course: dictionary
lesson: 10548
title: Alone or without others
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Read the words around a new word to find its meaning. Unaccompanied has the part un-, which means not, and accompanied, which means with someone, so it means not with someone.
explain: «A child flying alone, an unaccompanied minor, stays with the airline staff member who looks after them.» The words alone and looks after them are clues. Swap alone into the sentence and it still makes sense, so unaccompanied means without a parent or guardian with them.
explain: The same word works in music. When a choir sings unaccompanied, no instruments are playing with them. The meaning is still alone, just without other sounds.
fact: Unaccompanied means alone, without anyone going with you.
fact: An unaccompanied minor is a child travelling or staying somewhere without a parent or guardian.
fact: «No unaccompanied under-8s» is a sign that means small children must come with an adult.
fact: In music, unaccompanied means sung or played alone, without other instruments. This is also called a cappella.
fact: Unaccompanied is an adjective. It describes a noun, such as a child, a bag or a choir.
exercise: «A child flying alone, an unaccompanied minor, stays with the airline staff member who looks after them.» What does unaccompanied mean here? | *Without a parent or guardian with them | Happy and loud | Very tall and strong | Lost in the airport for good
exercise: A shop sign says «No unaccompanied under-8s». What does this mean? | *Small children must come with an adult | Small children can shop for free | The shop closes early for children | Only grown-ups can come in
exercise: Which word means a choir singing with no instruments playing? | nearby | *unaccompanied | luggage | cheerful
test: At an airport, a bag has no owner nearby. What is an unaccompanied bag? | *A bag left with no one looking after it | A bag that someone is carrying | A bag full of books | A bag that is the wrong colour
test: What should you do with an unaccompanied bag at an airport? | Open it and read the labels | *Report it to staff and do not touch it | Touch it to check what is inside | Take it to the lost property office yourself
exam: Which sentence uses unaccompanied correctly? | Unaccompanied is a colour of paint | The unaccompanied dog ran to the lake with its owner | *The little boy waited in the shop unaccompanied, so staff called his mum | The unaccompanied cake was full of cream and jam
